hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19153","Qutayba ibn Said narrated to us. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: And Qutayba ibn Said wrote it to me: I wrote to you in my hand and sealed the letter with my seal, its engraving: Allah is the patron of Said, may Allah have mercy on him, the seal of my father. Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Rabia, from Bakr ibn Sawada, from Muslim ibn Makhshi, from Ibn al-Firasi, that al-Firasi said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): May I beg? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No. And if you are one who asks inevitably, then ask the righteous."
